  "published": "2026-07-29T03:36:06.893Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "See CHANGELOG.md. 0.9.1 lowers the Windows App SDK requirement back to 2.2.1 — 0.9.0 wrongly required 2.3.2, which is higher than the WinUI the Microsoft.WindowsAppSDK meta-package provides, breaking framework-dependent apps. Prefer 0.9.1 over 0.9.0. Behavioural changes carried over from 0.9.0: the synchronous ParseHtml/LoadHtml/InsertHtml no longer download remote images (use the Async variants); AllowRemoteImagesOnPaste now also governs LoadHtml*/InsertHtml; turning a list off now clears its nesting level; RTF output reshaped for HWP/Word table and alignment fidelity. The control API may still change.",
